From: Helder Correia <heldercorreia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: stop opening every font in the DirectWrite font database

Two code paths opened every installed font file, each once per process.

populateFontDatabase() created an IDWriteFont for every installed font to
read its GDI-compatible and typographic family names. Creating a font opens
its file, so on a cold start with many fonts installed this blocked the
first use of any font for seconds: 8.7 s for 2681 fonts on Windows 11.

Read the same names from the font set of each family instead. Its
properties come from the system font cache. On the same machine and cold
start this took 11.6 ms and registered the same 1777 family names.

The style names collectAdditionalNames() also read were not used here.

fallbacksForFamily() called the default implementation, which populates
every family, and populating opens every font file. One requested family
that isn't installed, or one glyph the font lacks, therefore opened all
fonts on the GUI thread. It took 0.62 s for 359 font files and 0.35 s for
528, in warm starts on two Windows machines.

When the script has no writing system to filter by, every family is a
candidate, so the list needs only the family names. These are known without
populating, and QFontEngineMulti loads each fallback only when the ones
before it lack a glyph. Scripts with a writing system still use the default
implementation, which needs the writing system of each family.

With both changes, a warm start with 1766 families went from 3.03 s to
0.35 s and opened 16 font files instead of 1149, also when the requested
family wasn't installed.
---
--- a/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsdirectwritefontdatabase.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsdirectwritefontdatabase.cpp
@@ -389,7 +389,30 @@ QStringList QWindowsDirectWriteFontDatabase::fallbacksForFamily(const QString &f
     result.append(QWindowsFontDatabaseBase::familiesForScript(script));
     result.append(familyForStyleHint(styleHint));
     result.append(extraTryFontsForFamily(family));
-    result.append(QPlatformFontDatabase::fallbacksForFamily(family, style, styleHint, script));
+
+    const auto writingSystem = qt_writing_system_for_script(script);
+    if (writingSystem == QFontDatabase::Any
+        || writingSystem >= QFontDatabase::WritingSystemsCount) {
+        // Every family is a candidate here, so no family needs populating.
+        // QFontEngineMulti loads a fallback only when the ones before it lack
+        // a glyph, while populating every family opens every font file, which
+        // takes most of a second even when the first fallback has the glyph.
+        // Bitmap fonts go last, as in the default implementation.
+        auto *db = QFontDatabasePrivate::instance();
+        QStringList bitmapFamilies;
+        for (int i = 0; i < db->count; ++i) {
+            const QtFontFamily *f = db->families[i];
+            if (f->populated && f->count == 0)
+                continue;
+            if (m_populatedBitmapFonts.contains(f->name))
+                bitmapFamilies.append(f->name);
+            else
+                result.append(f->name);
+        }
+        result.append(bitmapFamilies);
+    } else {
+        result.append(QPlatformFontDatabase::fallbacksForFamily(family, style, styleHint, script));
+    }
 
     qCDebug(lcQpaFonts) << __FUNCTION__ << family << style << styleHint
         << script << result;
@@ -725,13 +748,36 @@ void QWindowsDirectWriteFontDatabase::populateFontDatabase()
                         registerFamily(englishLocaleName, QString{});
                 }
 
-                for (uint j = 0; j < fontFamily->GetFontCount(); ++j) {
-                    DirectWriteScope<IDWriteFont3> font;
-                    if (SUCCEEDED(fontFamily->GetFont(j, &font))) {
-                        collectAdditionalNames(*font,
-                                               hasDefaultLocale ? defaultLocale : nullptr,
-                                               englishLocale,
-                                               registerFamily);
+                // Read the GDI-compatible and typographic family names of each font
+                // from the family's font set. Font set properties come from the
+                // system font cache, while creating an IDWriteFont for every font
+                // opens its file, which takes seconds on a cold start when many
+                // fonts are installed. The style names are not needed here.
+                DirectWriteScope<IDWriteFontSet1> fontSet;
+                if (SUCCEEDED(fontFamily->GetFontSet(&fontSet))) {
+                    IDWriteFontSet *familyFonts = *fontSet;
+                    const DWRITE_FONT_PROPERTY_ID nameProperties[] = {
+                        DWRITE_FONT_PROPERTY_ID_WIN32_FAMILY_NAME,
+                        DWRITE_FONT_PROPERTY_ID_TYPOGRAPHIC_FAMILY_NAME
+                    };
+                    for (uint j = 0; j < familyFonts->GetFontCount(); ++j) {
+                        for (const DWRITE_FONT_PROPERTY_ID property : nameProperties) {
+                            BOOL exists = FALSE;
+                            DirectWriteScope<IDWriteLocalizedStrings> familyNames;
+                            if (FAILED(familyFonts->GetPropertyValues(j, property, &exists, &familyNames))
+                                || !exists || *familyNames == nullptr) {
+                                continue;
+                            }
+
+                            const QString englishName = localeString(*familyNames, englishLocale);
+                            if (!englishName.isEmpty())
+                                registerFamily(englishName, QString{});
+                            if (hasDefaultLocale) {
+                                const QString defaultName = localeString(*familyNames, defaultLocale);
+                                if (!defaultName.isEmpty())
+                                    registerFamily(defaultName, QString{});
+                            }
+                        }
                     }
                 }
             }
